275
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:44,520
The sport is called freeride.

276
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:49,760
And to try something like this, you better be riding the world's strongest bike.

277
00:23:50,820 --> 00:23:54,760
The technology has far surpassed most people's wildest imagination,

278
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:59,740
giving the riders the ability to go faster, to jump higher, to jump farther,

279
00:24:00,560 --> 00:24:04,480
and to be able to do it with far less pain and far less discomfort.

280
00:24:04,481 --> 00:24:11,060
Specialized in Morgan Hill, California, is a well-known builder of hardcore mountain

281
00:24:11,061 --> 00:24:13,060
bikes.

282
00:24:13,061 --> 00:24:20,000
Its vision of the world's strongest bike all comes down to a nearly invincible frame.

283
00:24:20,001 --> 00:24:23,160
They call it the Demo.

284
00:24:23,161 --> 00:24:28,520
Suggested retail price fully loaded, about $6,300.

285
00:24:28,521 --> 00:24:33,180
This is the Demo 8 frame, and it's the strongest bike in the world due to the construction.

286
00:24:33,181 --> 00:24:41,680
It's entirely aerospace-grade aluminum, which is a fantastic material because it allows us to manipulate the material into whatever shape we need for the strength.

287
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:43,680
We also use magnesium in some areas.

288
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:46,500
For example, this portion here is a very lightweight link.

289
00:24:46,980 --> 00:24:52,040
It's made out of cold-forged magnesium, so it's very, very light and also quite strong.

290
00:24:53,780 --> 00:24:58,120
The test lab it specialized is a house of horrors for a prototype bike frame.

291
00:24:58,121 --> 00:25:11,000
Technicians apply every conceivable type of fatigue and impact test over hundreds of hours to tubes, handlebars, and even pedals.

292
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:15,620
We want to make sure that these tests simulate what's happening in the field.

293
00:25:16,180 --> 00:25:20,480
There is no international standard for a downhill bike, so we had to make our own.

294
00:25:20,481 --> 00:25:25,620
We had to make sure that the demo is able to withstand the most heinous loads

295
00:25:25,621 --> 00:25:29,100
because these guys are doing things that nobody else is doing on their bikes.

296
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:33,220
This is a head tube ultimate strength test,

297
00:25:33,420 --> 00:25:36,660
and what we're going to simulate here is just a frontal impact.

298
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:42,160
This bike is going to be able to withstand at least six times what an actual rider can handle.

299
00:25:42,380 --> 00:25:47,220
We've seen that a rider gets actually ejected from the bike at about 15 miles an hour

300
00:25:47,221 --> 00:25:48,480
in a full-on frontal impact.

301
00:25:48,481 --> 00:25:53,320
A 500 pound per square inch front fork press tries to answer the question.

302
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:57,160
What kind of crash would break the world's strongest bike?

303
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:09,020
So we're talking about, you know, running into a wall head on at like 40 miles an hour,

304
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:11,840
which no human could even hold on to a bike anymore.

305
00:26:12,100 --> 00:26:14,840
So obviously this is well stronger than it needs to be.

306
00:26:14,841 --> 00:26:18,060
And it's proved because we've never actually seen a failure like this in the field.

307
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:25,360
After a strong frame, the other measure of bike strength and mastering big jumps is called travel.

308
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:31,420
Travel is a measurement that gauges the distance that the wheels can move up and down.

309
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:38,940
The demo suspension dissipates the energy absorbed by wheel impacts and cushions the rider.

310
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:43,900
The bigger the travel, the bigger the jumps a rider can survive.

311
00:26:43,901 --> 00:26:50,900
Top pros and their bikes have survived jumps equivalent to falling off a three-story building.

312
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:59,160
Most larger drops consist of anything from about 12 feet of vertical drop up to about maybe 35 feet.

313
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:06,180
The actual angle of the landing increases or decreases, and that determines how much impact you have on the landing.

314
00:27:07,220 --> 00:27:12,540
Before they make it into the hands of these top riders, the bike prototypes are performance tested.

315
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:18,900
A trip to the loading dock can offer engineers some real-world data in a hurry.

316
00:27:18,901 --> 00:27:23,900
This is a demo we've set up to measure loads from the field from riders.

317
00:27:23,901 --> 00:27:25,900
It's called a data acquisition bike.

318
00:27:25,901 --> 00:27:28,900
What we've done is attached tiny measurement devices.

319
00:27:28,901 --> 00:27:30,900
They're called strain gauges.

320
00:27:30,901 --> 00:27:35,900
What these do is measure the load that's applied from riding in each of these locations.

321
00:27:35,901 --> 00:27:38,900
And it connects to these wires, and it'll go up to this box,

322
00:27:38,901 --> 00:27:42,900
and while we're riding, it'll send all the information to this block right here.

323
00:27:42,901 --> 00:27:49,900
We can later download this to the computer and evaluate exactly what the rider experienced on the terrain.

324
00:27:51,900 --> 00:27:56,900
But a five-foot jump off a loading dock will only go so far.

325
00:28:00,900 --> 00:28:02,900
Well done.

326
00:28:02,901 --> 00:28:09,900
Engineers at Specialized often tap professional riders to test frames on the ladder course outside of town.

327
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:16,860
These test ramps help work out all the bugs before the competitions begin.

328
00:28:19,580 --> 00:28:22,320
Just 20 years ago, such jumps were unthinkable.

329
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:29,040
The Stump Jumper was Specialized's first mountain bike, and the first one mass-produced in the world.

330
00:28:30,380 --> 00:28:31,840
The early bikes were made of steel.

331
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:36,800
By switching to lighter, more malleable materials like carbon fiber and aluminum,

332
00:28:37,900 --> 00:28:40,040
today's bikes are up to 10 times stronger.

333
00:28:40,041 --> 00:28:47,040
Today Specialized has to face tough competition for the title of world's strongest bike.

334
00:28:47,041 --> 00:28:55,040
Fose Racing in Pasadena, California is a mom and pop bike shop on steroids.

335
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:09,040
While most of the larger companies outsource their manufacturing, Fose bikes are completely built by hand, in-house.

336
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:13,580
This is our new 2 to 1 DHS Mono downhill frame.

337
00:29:13,900 --> 00:29:16,860
I believe it's the world's strongest bike in production.

338
00:29:16,861 --> 00:29:20,820
It has our own design top tube, our down tube.

339
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:24,880
It's based around a 2 to 1 leverage ratio with our own shock that we designed,

340
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:28,500
and it works with the floating brake to eliminate any wheel hop.

341
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:30,740
And this bike is unstoppable.

342
00:29:31,740 --> 00:29:33,720
Tipping the scales at more than 40 pounds,

343
00:29:34,280 --> 00:29:36,420
with a retail price of around $6,000,

344
00:29:36,421 --> 00:29:41,182
dollars. The DHS Mono marries muscle to downhill gravity.

345
00:29:41,183 --> 00:29:44,440
It's like a motorcycle without a motor.

346
00:29:44,660 --> 00:29:48,280
I mean, you do have to pedal it, but you ride these things basically the same way,

347
00:29:48,340 --> 00:29:51,800
even though you don't have a throttle to get yourself out of trouble or whatever.

348
00:29:57,560 --> 00:30:05,061
In the Faux's suspension lap, the Mono is big. This is our new XTD downhill fork.

349
00:30:05,062 --> 00:30:06,080
The size is

350
00:30:06,081 --> 00:30:11,556
what gives us the strength and the rigidity and stiffness. Everything is big.

351
00:30:11,557 --> 00:30:12,480
30 millimeter

352
00:30:12,481 --> 00:30:14,885
axle, inch and a half inner fork legs.

353
00:30:14,886 --> 00:30:17,860
It feels like you've got power steering on your

354
00:30:17,861 --> 00:30:25,446
bike. A powerful frame begins from a thin sheet of aluminum.

355
00:30:25,447 --> 00:30:28,480
A water jet extracts the

356
00:30:28,481 --> 00:30:35,480
shapes, and a 5,000-pound hydraulic press forms the tube segments.

357
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:44,480
What we have here now is all the parts that it takes to complete this front triangle to

358
00:30:44,481 --> 00:30:45,465
our downhill frame.

359
00:30:45,466 --> 00:30:49,040
We'll put it in a welding fixture, we'll tack weld it together, we'll

360
00:30:49,041 --> 00:30:54,480
take it out, and then final weld it, and then it goes off to the heat treaters.

361
00:30:54,481 --> 00:30:57,780
Built for torture, FOSE bikes will take on all comers.

362
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:01,380
So which bike rules?

363
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:05,320
The FOSE Racing DHS Mono?

364
00:31:06,220 --> 00:31:07,940
Or the Specialized Demo?

365
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,660
The fact is, they're both plenty strong.

366
00:31:13,640 --> 00:31:16,060
So strong that when the elite prepare to jump,

367
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:19,700
it's less about the bike and more about the rider.

368
00:31:21,100 --> 00:31:22,820
There's always that what if, right?

369
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:24,420
What if I don't make it?

370
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:28,460
far enough, what if I come up short, you know, all those what else are going through your head

371
00:31:28,461 --> 00:31:32,940
and then you take off the lip, but once you're off, then it's all good and it's sheer exhilaration.

372
00:31:34,120 --> 00:31:36,860
These stunts test the limits of engineered strength.

373
00:31:38,560 --> 00:31:40,020
And so do these.

