00:31:53,361 --> 00:31:56,020
It could bear the weight of a Mini Cooper automobile.

378
00:31:57,660 --> 00:32:01,240
World's Strongest 3 will return on Modern Marvels.

379
00:32:04,700 --> 00:32:08,720
We now return to World's Strongest 3 on Modern Marvels.

380
00:32:10,660 --> 00:32:16,420
The USS Ronald Reagan may hold the powerlifting title with the world's strongest elevators at sea.

381
00:32:17,820 --> 00:32:21,560
But they only have one range of motion, up and down.

382
00:32:23,360 --> 00:32:31,780
If it's mind-boggling full-axis motion you're looking for, Cirque du Soleil holds the keys to the world's strongest stage elevator.

383
00:32:34,080 --> 00:32:37,160
It's the centerpiece of the Las Vegas production, Ka.

384
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:42,300
We're at the Ka Theater in the MGM Grand Hotel in Las Vegas.

385
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:47,320
We're standing on the Sand Cliff deck, which is one of seven moving platforms we have here at the show.

386
00:32:47,580 --> 00:32:51,460
This deck can lift, rotate, and tilt all at the same time.

387
00:32:51,461 --> 00:32:54,020
It does that in various combinations during the show.

388
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:56,120
What you see behind me is the audience,

389
00:32:56,380 --> 00:32:59,640
and as we move around, you'll see the various portions of the stage.

390
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:03,880
Measuring 6 feet thick and weighing 80,000 pounds,

391
00:33:04,860 --> 00:33:07,300
the Sand Cliff deck represents Cirque du Soleil's

392
00:33:07,301 --> 00:33:09,680
most ambitious technological challenge to date.

393
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:15,940
The entertainment consumer gets more and more sophisticated as time goes on.

394
00:33:16,240 --> 00:33:19,460
So it takes a little more to create the wow factor.

395
00:33:19,461 --> 00:33:24,120
And at Cirque du Soleil, we're constantly pushing the envelope of what is the wow factor.

396
00:33:25,260 --> 00:33:29,300
And part of that is pushing the physical limits of what we can do in a staged space.

397
00:33:29,900 --> 00:33:35,900
Pushing the limits meant engineering the strongest hydraulic gantry crane and deck in theatrical history.

398
00:33:37,460 --> 00:33:44,820
The crane and deck weigh 300,000 pounds combined, or about 136 million poker chips.

399
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:49,020
The platform is a full motion behemoth.

400
00:33:49,460 --> 00:33:53,700
that can lift, swivel, and hang 30 acrobats onto a vertical wall.

401
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:58,600
Now the crane is capable of moving at 2 feet per second vertically.

402
00:33:59,140 --> 00:34:04,140
It can spin continuously, and it can tilt 100 degrees towards the audience,

403
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:06,900
so it could dump me right into the basement at this point if we like.

404
00:34:07,700 --> 00:34:12,940
The sand cliff deck is visible to the audience, but the muscle behind it is out of sight.

405
00:34:14,460 --> 00:34:19,120
The deck is built on a mechanical extension arc with a tilting, rotating wrist.

406
00:34:19,460 --> 00:34:23,520
A hydraulic gantry crane raises and lowers the arm.

407
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:28,180
The gantry moves on rollers traveling on two massive columns,

408
00:34:29,580 --> 00:34:33,260
each one four feet in diameter and 100 feet tall.

409
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:38,820
The hydraulic cylinders that lift and tilt the crane were custom made for us.

410
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:41,440
These are the longest cylinders ever made in the world.

411
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:43,680
There's only two places in the world that can make them.

412
00:34:43,681 --> 00:34:48,840
We operate those cylinders in tension because we would bend that rod if we tried to push with it,

413
00:34:48,841 --> 00:34:53,980
So we pull up the crane, and those cylinders actually extend right out through the roof of the theater.

414
00:34:55,500 --> 00:35:01,180
When engineers built the Sandcliffe deck at MGM Grand, they knew it was a brute force proposition.

415
00:35:02,920 --> 00:35:07,560
Moving it requires 2,000 horsepower and a little vegetable oil.

416
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:10,360
We're in the hydraulic pump from now.

417
00:35:10,960 --> 00:35:13,380
Behind me are five 250-horsepower pumps.

418
00:35:13,381 --> 00:35:15,960
There are two pumps actually on each motor.

419
00:35:18,840 --> 00:35:24,640
When we walk around this way, we'll see the hydraulic reservoir.

420
00:35:24,641 --> 00:35:28,520
This is a double-walled tank that holds 4,000 gallons of vegetable oil.

421
00:35:28,521 --> 00:35:32,140
The fire department didn't want us to have real hydraulic oil in the room, so we went

422
00:35:32,141 --> 00:35:34,340
with vegetable oil, which is non-flammable.

423
00:35:34,341 --> 00:35:38,080
On the other side of the room, we have nitrogen banks and piston accumulators.

424
00:35:38,081 --> 00:35:42,400
These actually store the energy from the pump, so we use the pumps as rather like a battery

425
00:35:42,401 --> 00:35:44,840
charger to charge the accumulator banks.

426
00:35:44,841 --> 00:35:48,800
The accumulators actually push the oil out into the theater at up to 2,000 gallons a

427
00:35:48,801 --> 00:35:52,400
minute to operate the crane.

428
00:35:52,401 --> 00:35:58,300
The long pipes needed to push the hydraulic oil are located on the theater's roof.

429
00:35:58,301 --> 00:36:04,940
An automation technician monitors pressure and initiates all Sandcliffe deck moves.

430
00:36:04,941 --> 00:36:07,440
Precisely timed audio cues drive the action.

431
00:36:07,441 --> 00:36:11,440
Standby, turn sister in.

432
00:36:11,441 --> 00:36:13,440
Make the train clear.

433
00:36:13,441 --> 00:36:18,620
So right now we're beginning the show.

434
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:20,620
This is what we call the music box.

435
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:24,740
It introduces the gantry crane to the audience in the form of a vessel.

436
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:28,100
This hefty deck does a lot more than just move.

437
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,500
It's loaded with surprises.

438
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:37,020
We have 80 pegs that appear when artists pretend to shoot arrows at the stage.

439
00:36:37,600 --> 00:36:40,900
Those pegs are then used as acrobatic handholds in a scene.

440
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:50,340
Later on, the pegs extend at another distance and are used as rock climbing handholds in the cliff scene.

441
00:36:50,540 --> 00:36:55,540
The entire surface of that deck is a capacitive touchscreen as well,

442
00:36:55,720 --> 00:37:01,160
in that the artist's position on the deck interacts with the video projection during the show.

443
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:04,560
Sharp eyes keep a close watch on the deck's movements.

444
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:08,520
A sudden pressure loss could spell disaster.

445
00:37:08,521 --> 00:37:13,980
At this station, I monitor all the hydraulic controls and all the show operation,

446
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:17,240
as well as what everybody in the automation department is doing.

